{"c":[{"id":"cd14b8843dd9d3ee","sum":"C1-I6: a WARNS-word sentence goes whole or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off (no executor step); an Ask reads the tab left only at its fill step or pagePlan; ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone; the hourly budget holds pageWalked.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2691af9702ea9f68","sum":"C1-I6: a value whose sentence holds a WARNS word goes with it as a required clause or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off step ('You press <label>' / 'The rest is yours') with no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032641Z-df47ef2e50ca5a79","text":"C1: a value whose own sentence holds a WARNS word goes with that sentence as a required clause or not at all; sentence ends are conservative (lowercase word or digit before, capital after). Whole-line clauses cost corpus clinic-intake two values.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062218Z-bb39f9f0467bc5ce","text":"I6: page plans end with a GoalStep row:true (kind handoff, 'You press <label>' or 'The rest is yours'); it is always the last step, lower.ts gives it no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter than seg.steps.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"740e3d49bc3a2762","sum":"I6: an Ask reads the tab left only at planAsk's fill step or pagePlan (owner: offer key or goal id); ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone (goalOnPage); the hourly budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T062227Z-47ccc650cd567ff8","text":"I6: an Ask's tab read happens only at planAsk's fill step (fillModel) or in pagePlan; owners are the offer key or goal id; ambient fill/ready-on-load leave a page with a planning/awaiting/running goal alone (goalOnPage) and TabSource refuses an ambient read over a pinned goal.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-6c026cce4f5fd842","text":"I6: page-loop-eval runs every page in one helper; the hourly offer budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked before the ready-on-load check, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour; fill.load_held_<rule> counts holds.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c154314373edc26c","sum":"H11-H12: host.sock in <home>/sockets, release answers state+spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; route page-engine test apply to its own helper; .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wrapped panels (exact width); never lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5e0b1d7fe48d167f","sum":"H12-I6: host.sock is <home>/sockets/host.sock; release builds answer only state and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full (harnesses setenv it); onboarding auto only without --home/--settings; helper page-engine tests route apply to their own helper.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T035452Z-68fb99dd307065d5","text":"H12: host.sock moved to <home>/sockets/host.sock (default CaretV2/sockets); release builds answer only state (allowlist) and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full, so release-build harnesses must setenv it. Onboarding defaults to auto only without --home/--settings.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-7e02cffa1979776c","text":"I6: helper tests with a page engine must route its apply to their own helper (capture it in a local); a shared 'helper' variable lets an earlier test's trailing walk land in the next test's model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"86a6db3d2adf8e6a","sum":"H11: under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) wrapped text measures as one line and panels clip: use an exact .frame(width:) with vertical fixedSize; build.lock is a symlink to heavy.lock, so lockf build.lock inside with-heavy deadlocks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T063851Z-1e89e23b19f1384e","text":"H11: a SwiftUI view under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) is measured at its ideal width, so wrapped text counts as one line and the panel clips its top and bottom; give it an exact .frame(width:) and fixedSize(vertical) only (PopupView PopupWidth).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T063851Z-3a51e09ec56311ba","text":"H11: ~/.caret-run/locks/build.lock is a symlink to ~/.long-run/locks/heavy.lock; wrapping lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.sh (which holds heavy.lock) deadlocks while holding the heavy lease.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
